{"questions":[{"question_id":"luxzq9e3","content":"<p>Match List I with List II</p>\n<p>\n<table class=\"tg\" style=\"undefined;table-layout: fixed; width: 572px\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 75px\">\n<col style=\"width: 160px\">\n<col style=\"width: 75px\">\n<col style=\"width: 262px\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">LIST I<br>(Test)</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">LIST II<br>(Observation)</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">A.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> water test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">I.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Yellow orange or orange red precipitate formed</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">B.\t</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Ceric ammonium nitrate test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">II.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Reddish orange colour disappears</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">C.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Ferric chloride test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">III.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Red colour appears</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">D.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">2, 4 - DNP test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">IV.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Blue, Green, Violet or Red colour appear</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 9th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pmatch-list-i-with-list-iip-pstyle-typetextcss-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-hev9mcesx1vgtqbk","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Match List I with List II</p>\n<p>\n<table class=\"tg\" style=\"undefined;table-layout: fixed; width: 572px\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 75px\">\n<col style=\"width: 160px\">\n<col style=\"width: 75px\">\n<col style=\"width: 262px\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">LIST I<br>(Test)</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">LIST II<br>(Observation)</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">A.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> water test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">I.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Yellow orange or orange red precipitate formed</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">B.\t</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Ceric ammonium nitrate test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">II.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Reddish orange colour disappears</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">C.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Ferric chloride test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">III.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Red colour appears</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">D.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">2, 4 - DNP test</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">IV.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">Blue, Green, Violet or Red colour appear</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Let's match the given tests in List I with the correct observations in List II based on known chemical reactions and their typical outcomes:</p>\n\n<p> List I with List II</p>\n\n<strong>A. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> water test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used to detect unsaturation in organic compounds. If the compound has a double bond (alkenes) or a triple bond (alkynes), the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> in water (bromine water) will react and decolorize.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Reddish orange color of bromine water disappears (II).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>B. Ceric ammonium nitrate test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used to detect alcohols. Ceric ammonium nitrate forms a red-colored complex with alcohols.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Red color appears (III).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>C. Ferric chloride test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>Commonly used to detect phenols, the ferric chloride test leads to the formation of a colored complex with phenols, typically varying shades like purple, green, blue, or even red, depending on the specific phenol.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Blue, Green, Violet, or Red color appear (IV).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>D. 2,4-DNP test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used for the detection of carbonyl compounds (aldehydes and ketones). 2,4-Dinitrophenylhydrazine (2,4-DNP) reacts with carbonyl groups to form a yellow, orange, or red precipitate.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Yellow orange or orange red precipitate formed (I).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Conclusion:</p>\n\n<p>Based on these observations, the correct matching of tests with outcomes should be:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A with II</li><br>\n<li>B with III</li><br>\n<li>C with IV</li><br>\n<li>D with I</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This makes the correct choice:</p>\n\n<strong>Option A: A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I</strong>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>सूची I का मिलान सूची II से करेः</p>\n<p>\n<table class=\"tg\" style=\"undefined;table-layout: fixed; width: 618px\"><colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 78px\">\n<col style=\"width: 206px\">\n<col style=\"width: 83px\">\n<col style=\"width: 251px\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">सूची I<br>(परीक्षण)</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-7btt\">सूची II<br>(प्रेक्षण)</th>\n  </tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(A)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> जल परीक्षण</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(I)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">पीला-नारंगी या नारंगी-लाल अवक्षेप बनता है।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(B)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">सेरिक अमोनियम नाइट्रेट परीक्षण</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(II)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">लाल-नारंगी रंग गायब हो जाता है।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(C)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">फेरिक क्लोराइड परीक्षण</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(III)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">लाल रंग उत्पन्न होता है।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(D)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">2,4 - DNP परीक्षण</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-c3ow\">(IV)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0pky\">नीला, हरा, बैंगनी या लाल रंग उत्पन्न होता है।</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table></p>\n<p>नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर को चुनेः</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>आइए सूची I में दिए गए परीक्षणों को सूची II में सही प्रेक्षणों के साथ ज्ञात रासायनिक अभिक्रियाओं और उनके विशिष्ट परिणामों के आधार पर सुमेलित करें:</p>\n\n<p>सूची I को सूची II के साथ सुमेलित करना</p>\n\n<strong>A. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> जल परीक्षण</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>यह परीक्षण कार्बनिक यौगिकों में असंतृप्तता का पता लगाने के लिए उपयोग किया जाता है। यदि यौगिक में द्विबंध (ऐल्कीन) या त्रिबंध (ऐल्काइन) है, तो जल में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (ब्रोमीन जल) अभिक्रिया करके विरंजित हो जाएगा।</li><br>\n<li><strong>सही प्रेक्षण:</strong> ब्रोमीन जल का लाल-नारंगी रंग गायब हो जाता है (II)।</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>B. सेरिक अमोनियम नाइट्रेट परीक्षण</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>यह परीक्षण ऐल्कोहॉल का पता लगाने के लिए उपयोग किया जाता है। सेरिक अमोनियम नाइट्रेट ऐल्कोहॉल के साथ लाल रंग का संकुल बनाता है।</li><br>\n<li><strong>सही प्रेक्षण:</strong> लाल रंग प्रकट होता है (III)।</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>C. फेरिक क्लोराइड परीक्षण</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>फीनॉल का पता लगाने के लिए सामान्यतः उपयोग किया जाता है, फेरिक क्लोराइड परीक्षण फीनॉल के साथ रंगीन संकुल का निर्माण करता है, जो विशिष्ट फीनॉल के आधार पर बैंगनी, हरा, नीला, या लाल जैसे विभिन्न रंगों में हो सकता है।</li><br>\n<li><strong>सही प्रेक्षण:</strong> नीला, हरा, बैंगनी, या लाल रंग प्रकट होता है (IV)।</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>D. 2,4-DNP परीक्षण</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>यह परीक्षण कार्बोनिल यौगिकों (ऐल्डिहाइड और कीटोन) का पता लगाने के लिए उपयोग किया जाता है। 2,4-डाइनाइट्रोफेनिलहाइड्रेज़ीन (2,4-DNP) कार्बोनिल समूहों के साथ अभिक्रिया करके पीला, नारंगी, या लाल अवक्षेप बनाता है।</li><br>\n<li><strong>सही प्रेक्षण:</strong> पीला नारंगी या नारंगी लाल अवक्षेप बनता है (I)।</li>\n</ul>\n<p>निष्कर्ष:</p>\n\n<p>इन प्रेक्षणों के आधार पर, परीक्षणों का परिणामों के साथ सही सुमेलन होना चाहिए:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A के साथ II</li><br>\n<li>B के साथ III</li><br>\n<li>C के साथ IV</li><br>\n<li>D के साथ I</li>\n</ul>\n<p>यह सही विकल्प बनाता है:</p>\n\n<strong>विकल्प A: A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I</strong>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"chemistry-involved-in-the-preparation-of-organic-and-inorganic-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["matching_table"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-9th-april-evening-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>Let's match the given tests in List I with the correct observations in List II based on known chemical reactions and their typical outcomes:</p>\n\n<p> List I with List II</p>\n\n<strong>A. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> water test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used to detect unsaturation in organic compounds. If the compound has a double bond (alkenes) or a triple bond (alkynes), the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> in water (bromine water) will react and decolorize.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Reddish orange color of bromine water disappears (II).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>B. Ceric ammonium nitrate test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used to detect alcohols. Ceric ammonium nitrate forms a red-colored complex with alcohols.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Red color appears (III).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>C. Ferric chloride test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>Commonly used to detect phenols, the ferric chloride test leads to the formation of a colored complex with phenols, typically varying shades like purple, green, blue, or even red, depending on the specific phenol.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Blue, Green, Violet, or Red color appear (IV).</li>\n</ul>\n<br><strong>D. 2,4-DNP test</strong>\n\n<br><br><ul>\n<li>This test is used for the detection of carbonyl compounds (aldehydes and ketones). 2,4-Dinitrophenylhydrazine (2,4-DNP) reacts with carbonyl groups to form a yellow, orange, or red precipitate.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Correct Observation:</strong> Yellow orange or orange red precipitate formed (I).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Conclusion:</p>\n\n<p>Based on these observations, the correct matching of tests with outcomes should be:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A with II</li><br>\n<li>B with III</li><br>\n<li>C with IV</li><br>\n<li>D with I</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This makes the correct choice:</p>\n\n<strong>Option A: A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I</strong>"}]}